window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b107-bf787767823b71f9.json"]={sha256:"bf787767823b71f957cdee0831dcfce5b30dc12ae7b376d0b9f97762bb1c3987",value:{"id":"b107","title":"費馬恩海峽沉管隧道","titleEn":"Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"費馬恩海峽的官方工程頁列18公里沉管隧道，並記載2020年開始施工。本課以跨國道路鐵路共同走廊為背景，逐步檢查箱體量產、重量帳、海床支承、止水接頭和設備交付。未來營運效益與施工進度分開表述，不把建設中的設施描述為已完成營運。","summaryEn":"The official Fehmarnbelt project page describes an 18 km immersed tunnel and construction beginning in 2020. Using a cross-border road and rail corridor, this course examines element production, mass balance, seabed support, sealing and equipment handover. Future service benefits remain separate from construction progress; the facility is not described as already operational.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["頂板跨中彎矩","Roof-span bending"],["剩餘浮力","Residual buoyancy"],["止水壓縮餘量","Gasket compression reserve"],["擴散特徵長度","Diffusion characteristic length"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","頂板跨中彎矩","剩餘浮力","止水壓縮餘量","擴散特徵長度"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Roof-span bending","Residual buoyancy","Gasket compression reserve","Diffusion characteristic length"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「矩形沉管的框架受力」，再獨立計算「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」。原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為39.0202 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate rectangular immersed-box frame action, then independently calculate joint compression and sealing envelope. Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 39.0202 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b107-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「矩形沉管的框架受力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b107-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=14.4 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為15.84 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 15.84 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=14.4 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為15.84 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 15.84 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b107-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b107-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b107-v14-05","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「頂板跨中彎矩」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roof-span bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頂板跨中彎矩」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame. A circular thin-ring membrane formula is inappropriate. A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roof-span bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頂板跨中彎矩」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roof-span bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-05-k1","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action","text":"費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。","textEn":"Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" is correct?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b107-v14-06","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：定量估算","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂板跨中彎矩」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roof-span bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為39.0202 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 39.0202 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為39.0202 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 39.0202 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「矩形沉管的框架受力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b107-v14-07","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂板跨中彎矩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roof-span bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b107-v14-08","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂板跨中彎矩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roof-span bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。","textEn":"Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「矩形沉管的框架受力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b107-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」與「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" and \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-09","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「拘束溫度應變」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrained thermal strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拘束溫度應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension. Compressive-strength compliance does not establish crack resistance because modulus development, creep, gradients and pour sequence influence restraint. A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained thermal strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拘束溫度應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained thermal strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-09-k1","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking","text":"管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。","textEn":"Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" is correct?","options":["管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b107-v14-10","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拘束溫度應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrained thermal strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.15 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.15 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.15 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.15 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b107-v14-11","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拘束溫度應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrained thermal strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","failure":"注意干擾：只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b107-v14-12","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拘束溫度應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained thermal strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。","textEn":"Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b107-v14-13","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「剩餘浮力」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual buoyancy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents. A mass balance determines net vertical force but does not establish towing stability. Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual buoyancy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual buoyancy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-13-k1","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability","text":"費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。","textEn":"Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" is correct?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b107-v14-14","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual buoyancy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14640.4 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14640.4 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14640.4 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14640.4 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b107-v14-15","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual buoyancy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","failure":"注意干擾：只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\"?","options":["以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b107-v14-16","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual buoyancy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。","textEn":"Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b107-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「基床變形與接頭轉角」與「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" and \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-17","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷梯度」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact. Small total settlement does not imply small joint rotation; differential movement and support length control local distortion. Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-17-k1","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation","text":"海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。","textEn":"Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" is correct?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b107-v14-18","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：定量估算","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0471429 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0471429 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0471429 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0471429 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基床變形與接頭轉角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b107-v14-19","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","failure":"注意干擾：落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b107-v14-20","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。","textEn":"Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基床變形與接頭轉角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b107-v14-21","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-21-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b107-v14-22","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b107-v14-23","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b107-v14-24","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b107-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b107-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0515803 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0515803 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0515803 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0515803 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b107-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b107-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b107-v14-29","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「擴散特徵長度」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffusion characteristic length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「擴散特徵長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions. A square-root diffusion length indicates a time scale, not a corrosion-threshold depth. Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffusion characteristic length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「擴散特徵長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffusion characteristic length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-29-k1","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation","text":"海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。","textEn":"Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" is correct?","options":["擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b107-v14-30","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擴散特徵長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffusion characteristic length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.0759 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.0759 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.0759 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.0759 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b107-v14-31","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擴散特徵長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffusion characteristic length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","failure":"注意干擾：接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b107-v14-32","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擴散特徵長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffusion characteristic length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。","textEn":"Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b107-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b107-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為587 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 587 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為587 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 587 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b107-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode."],"answer":2,"explanation":"各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b107-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b107-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b107-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.3962 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.3962 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.3962 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.3962 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b107-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b107-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
